    "question": {
      ":question/id": "30778945-23df-50b0-95ba-a8bed6b6d058",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices have a rank of $3?$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 4 & 0 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 8 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 2 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & -6\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that a matrix of rank $3$ must have at least $3$ columns and at least $3$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the matrix $B$ since it has only $2$ rows. \n\nAlso, the matrix must have $3$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $A$ has exactly $3$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(A)=3.$ As we can see, the matrix $C$ has only $2$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(C)=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ only.\"",
